{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil","id":1043865,"title":"Repairing the Veil","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-04T22:33:19-08:00","id":1043865,"title":"Repairing the Veil","content":"So, I had a question about how do you repair the Veil. There are three primary threats to the Veil. First, leaving physical evidence behind after a kill (claw and fang marks, blood, fur, and saliva). Second, leaving photographic evidence (such as people snapping pictures or security cameras taking videos). Third, eyewitnesses who are strong willed enough to suppress the Delirium.<br /> <br /> In the first case, it is easy avoided by using weapons and attacking from stealth. While werewolves have superhuman stealth, the wounds from an ax fetich swung by a Garou in Glabro is similar enough to the wounds from ax swung by a psycho on PCP that no one will think 'supernatural' creature. If you slip up, you can repair the Veil by contaminating the evidence.<br /> <br /> In the second case, you can prevent detection by running around in any form except Crinos. If you get caught on film in Crinos, you can destroy the film or corrupt the files to repair the Veil.<br /> <br /> In the third case, there is a temptation to kill the witnesses, but that is probably a bad idea. People spouting nonsense about werewolves can be easily ignored. People spouting nonsense about werewolves and then being butchered by wolves gives legitimacy to their claims. The way to repair the Veil is to discredit the witnesses by making them seem insane so that other people will not be believed if they come forward.<br /> <br /> What other risks to the Veil can you think of and what are the correct (abound incorrect) ways your characters have dealt with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T02:10:28-08:00","id":1043892,"title":"","content":"On that matter, which tribe would be more typically &quot;in charge&quot; of the clean up process?<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs have Desk Jobs at Television Stations? Shadow Lords leading Forensic Teams made of Dirty Cops? Glass Walker Wise-Guys who make offers that witnesses &quot;can't refuse&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T08:21:44-08:00","id":1043992,"title":"","content":"Money.<br /> <br /> Discredit the person so people think they are crazy.<br /> <br /> Murder.<br /> <br /> Convince them you are the good guys and recruit them to your cause (rare, but may be worth the effort if they are lost kinfolk)<br /> <br /> Blame the incident on Ergot poisoning or whatever the modern equivalent would be. <br /> <br /> I imagine each Sept would be in charge of dealing with the issue themselves. Glasswalkers would be my first thought for clean up, but I imagine any technologically minded Kinfolk could do just as well. <br /> <br /> <br /> I have this possible plot point I may use in my quest. A Red Talon Sept has members who broke the &quot;don't eat people&quot; line of the Litany. Unfortunately, the people they ate were young college aged hikers. So now you have a major search going on for the college girls, which is all over national news. Nothing werewolfy in the news... yet. A CoG Lupus relative of the PC's pack has been sent to find the Litany Breakers and wants the PC's pack to come along to assist with the Human side of the situation. And the Human side will be Reporters, FBI Agents, and Hunters, oh my!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:12:44-08:00","id":1044013,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the major problem for the local Garou is that there is likely physical evidence, since Red Talons are rarely educated enough to possess the knowledge of forensic anthropology needed to clean up all the evidence. Unsolved murders occur because they usually happen to people the authorities do not care about. When you have something that high profile, they are probably going to find evidence of a kill by canines.<br /> <br /> The best case sceneries for that situation is to drag the Red Talon to Erebus and toss him in the Silver Lake as a preventive measure before repairing the Veil. Find a few feral dogs, infect them with rabies, and shoot them near the remains of one of the girls. The news story is 'Rapid dogs kill college girls' rather than 'Wolf pack kills college girls'. You can even have experts coming on TV talking about the dangers of feral dogs to humans when compared to the peaceful relations of wild wolves with humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:32:23-08:00","id":1044025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044013#post1044013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the major problem for the local Garou is that there is likely physical evidence, since Red Talons are rarely educated enough to possess the knowledge of forensic anthropology needed to clean up all the evidence. Unsolved murders occur because they usually happen to people the authorities do not care about. When you have something that high profile, they are probably going to find evidence of a kill by canines.<br /> <br /> The best case sceneries for that situation is to drag the Red Talon to Erebus and toss him in the Silver Lake as a preventive measure before repairing the Veil. Find a few feral dogs, infect them with rabies, and shoot them near the remains of one of the girls. The news story is 'Rapid dogs kill college girls' rather than 'Wolf pack kills college girls'. You can even have experts coming on TV talking about the dangers of feral dogs to humans when compared to the peaceful relations of wild wolves with humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>The PCs first job will be to take care of the evidence. &quot;Go find the murder site while I go sniff these Red Talon Assholes.&quot; <br /> <br /> The whole situation is a big mess which makes it a perfect plot for an RPG. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:39:38-08:00","id":1044028,"title":"","content":"Repairing the Veil is much easier in older times than now with modern forensics. The idea that a werewolf attack can be disguised as psychos on PCP won't hold up to any kind of crime scene investigation in 2017. This will probably confuse the police more than cause them to suspect werewolfery, but there is a much higher risk that evidence is going to fall into the hands of real dangers to the Garou - vampires with influence in the Police, various kinds of hunters, etc.<br /> <br /> PCs tend to do stupid things in regards to the Veil because players prioritize what is fun to do at the moment over concern for the Veil. In more realistic cases, Garou cubs have probably been very well instructed to prioritize the Veil as the first or second most important part of the Litany and been told lots of examples of what happens when the Veil is broken. So that means they handle situations with a care. Prevention, not repair, is the most effective means.<br /> <br /> But this doesn't answer the question. So what can be done in a modern concept? The below aren't necessarily things the PCs can do, but they are probably things a sept as whole can do.<br /> <br /> 1) Many things are now digitized. If you can't physically remove the evidence, you can try to hide it digitally by asking Weaver spirits on the web to remove files, make them inaccessible, alter them, etc. Glass Walker Theurges are probably highly in demand. I wouldn't be surprised if there was some kind of Glass Walker forensics institute whose full time job is to handle requests for the entire Garou Nation to assist various septs to do that. In fact, I would not be surprised if there aren't many kinds of Garou Nation level resources staffed by Silver Fangs, Glass Walkers, and others (and their kinfolk) to act as support for the Nation as a whole to do various things when septs themselves are overwhelmed. (This is probably an under explored area of the setting).<br /> <br /> 2) Ruin the evidence to make it useless. Cause a water pipe to explode in the evidence room. Start a fire from an electrical short. Cause an electrical black out in the city blocks where the evidence is kept. Summon rats and vermin to invade the place. These are highly suspect things in and of themselves and can't be used willy nilly, but in some extreme circumstances they can be warranted.<br /> <br /> 3) Make placement of kinfolk in key institutions (police, hospitals, government) a priority. Hopefully that kinfolk can be put in charge of the investigation and/or crime lab. Even kinfolk technical experts who could be retained by the police department for consulting, or called by lawyers to appear in court to discredit evidence would be useful.<br /> <br /> 4) Have fall guys ready. If there is a psycho on PCP ready at the time some Garou kill people, then unleash that psycho right now and have the police gun him down. That way the investigation ends quickly before all the evidence can be analyzed quickly. This is something the Bone Gnawer tribe might be good at - finding potential patsies to blame things on. Of course there would be some ethical dilemmas involved, but the Garou have done worse on the behalf of Gaia.<br /> <br /> 5) Come up with your own semi-plausible theories of why these things happen without reference to werewolves,and get them established as accepted explanations in the WoD setting. Maybe there are urban legends, psychiatric illnesses, bacterial spoilage and other kinds of contamination, used to explain these things. They don't really exist, but they are believed to be real in the WoD because of some very hard work by the collective Garou Nation over the years.<br /> <br /> 6) Special kinds of spirits that can eliminate or destroy evidence. This is perhaps the easiest thing to do especially for PCs. In fact, I've seen a few chronicles that have some kind of version like this so Garou and Wyrm minions can summon these spirits and protect the Veil. <br /> <br /> The best way I know to get PCs to act appropriately is to make sure they suffer punishments because of their actions. Make them lose renown. Deny them access to the caern for a while. Send hunters or Wyrm creatures after them. Make their pack totem angry with them. Once they pay a real penalty, they typically act better afterwards. The players typically aren't happy about it though so expect some complaints!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:39:59-08:00","id":1044029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044013#post1044013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, the major problem for the local Garou is that there is likely physical evidence, since Red Talons are rarely educated enough to possess the knowledge of forensic anthropology needed to clean up all the evidence. Unsolved murders occur because they usually happen to people the authorities do not care about. When you have something that high profile, they are probably going to find evidence of a kill by canines.</div> </div> </div> </div>The chances of humans finding the kill sight in the vast openness of a Red Talon protectorate is slim at best. The <i>may</i> be physical evidence around, but I really do think you underestimate the Talons. It is far more likely that the Hunters (experienced in the Supernatural) are going to find something than any of the normal humans. And since this is talking about a Talon Sept, that means the Elders are going to end up involved. I think the CoG Lupus is going to have their work cut out for them, given that the Sept is going to be closing ranks around the offender. This seems like it will be a much bigger deal from the Garou side of things. But really, the PCs (it sounds like) are there to run interference for the humans. And they will probably end up having to stand between the Sept and the humans for both of their protection. And the Sept certainly isn't going to appreciate it, having outsiders step in and think they know best how to protect the Caern from humans. <br /> <br /> Sounds like fun drama all around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044013#post1044013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The best case sceneries for that situation is to drag the Red Talon to Erebus and toss him in the Silver Lake as a preventive measure before repairing the Veil. Find a few feral dogs, infect them with rabies, and shoot them near the remains of one of the girls. The news story is 'Rapid dogs kill college girls' rather than 'Wolf pack kills college girls'. You can even have experts coming on TV talking about the dangers of feral dogs to humans when compared to the peaceful relations of wild wolves with humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hundreds of thousands of people go missing each year in the US. Most are found, but there are still a couple of thousand that disappear (every year) without a trace. The best case scenario is to just keep any investigators away from any helpful information. After a few weeks things will die down and the 90% of people with interest (generally all except for the Hunters) in searching for the kids will go home. That's the easiest way to manage it.<br /> There is next to no shot the Sept lets you send it's member to Erebus. So that idea should be right out unless you want to go toe to toe with a Talon Elder (you don't). <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:56:18-08:00","id":1044040,"title":"","content":"Erebus is a great resource though for the Garou Nation, as it lets them recycle the guilty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:21:20-08:00","id":1044053,"title":"","content":"To go off topic for a bit, what rank would you make the CoG Lupus Philodox?<br /> <br /> I envisioned him Athro, because he travels around to various Septs as an impartial judge. I always see Tribal Elders being more stationary. He's an old wolf, about fifty to sixty years old. He was born to the Black Furies so technically, he has no Pure Breed. He speaks-but not reads- more human languages than most homids. (&quot;What the fuck does the wolf know about anything?&quot; &quot;Don't underestimate Democritus. He speaks more languages than you do.&quot; ) When he is not traveling, he considers the PC's Texas Sept his home (He lets the Adrens run things and only offers assistance when asked). He doesn't have a pack of his own, but when needed he can nip some Garou on their shoulders and form a pack for the needs of the situation.<br /> <br /> If there is going to be Elder Red Talons involved, would the CoG/Garou Nation want to send Elders of their own?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-05-2017, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:42:47-08:00","id":1044071,"title":"","content":"The Red Talons are the smallest Tribe, so one of their Septs would be given minimal honors in my opinion. With 1280 Garou in the USA (assuming a population ratio of 1:250,000 for the USA), there might be 40 Red Talons divided among 8 Red Talon Septs in the USA (Garou are exceptionally rare in cWoD). I doubt that there will be more than four Red Talon Elders in the USA, so why bother sending one of your Elders to deal problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T11:54:26-08:00","id":1044113,"title":"","content":"A universal Human to Garou Ratio isn't really a thing... like at all, that is more a vampire thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T12:18:23-08:00","id":1044130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044053#post1044053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To go off topic for a bit, what rank would you make the CoG Lupus Philodox?<br /> <br /> I envisioned him Athro, because he travels around to various Septs as an impartial judge. I always see Tribal Elders being more stationary. He's an old wolf, about fifty to sixty years old. He was born to the Black Furies so technically, he has no Pure Breed. He speaks-but not reads- more human languages than most homids. (&quot;What the fuck does the wolf know about anything?&quot; &quot;Don't underestimate Democritus. He speaks more languages than you do.&quot; ) When he is not traveling, he considers the PC's Texas Sept his home (He lets the Adrens run things and only offers assistance when asked). He doesn't have a pack of his own, but when needed he can nip some Garou on their shoulders and form a pack for the needs of the situation.<br /> <br /> If there is going to be Elder Red Talons involved, would the CoG/Garou Nation want to send Elders of their own?</div> </div> </div> </div>So with all due respect, I would ignore <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>'s numbers. Story-wise, this is a Red Talon Sept and so it should be filled with Talons and Kinfolk. What level is the Caern? That will give you an idea of how many Garou you have there. That's all that really matters on that part of this story.<br /> <br /> For your CoG being Athro, that makes sense. I would have said Rank 4-5 depending on need. If he is well known among the Garou of the region/continent (especially for this sort of role) then they shouldn't need backup going into the Sept, especially with him being Lupus. Without knowing any more details, I would imagine him announcing himself and then talking to the Sept Elder(s) directly. With him explaining what happened, and what the humans know and what he expects will come to the area because of it. His best bet will be to be direct and sincere (since he is) and offer his help, however unwanted. Most of this will play out off screen since I imagine the PCs will be busy doing their own thing on the human side for him. If you have a Lupus in the group, you can have them accompany your CoG if you or they want to. <br /> <br /> Either way, this CoG should be afforded the respect he deserves (for his Rank and reputation) and after some contention should be able to get the Talons to police their own. Especially since their actions have brought unwanted human attention to the area. He may even be involved in doling out the punishment Rites. Up to you. For the humans venturing into the area, Trackless Waste will handle the majority of them. And 1-2 members of the Sept probably have it.<br /> <br /> So yea, that leaves your players to run around the local towns and run interference where they can, and maybe to end up standing between some of the lower rank Sept members and their trying to drive off the humans. Possibly even coming into contact with the guilty Garou haphazardly trying to cover their mistake. The Talon Caern may even end up paying for the Litany-breaker's mistake by having a wolf hunt called in the area if things go that far and the humans suspect wolves for killing the hikers. That though, would end up being one of the worst case scenarios, as that means that everyone failed in what they needed to do (the CoG, the Sept and the PC pack).<br /> <br /> Again, sounds like a fun story setup. Lots of chances for things to go wrong, but lots of different ways to go about getting through it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T13:38:38-08:00","id":1044153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044113#post1044113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A universal Human to Garou Ratio isn't really a thing... like at all, that is more a vampire thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>Annnnd that is all that really needs to be said on the matter-<br /> <br /> Since Red Talons keep coming up, that tribe has a few ways of employing gifts to protect the Veil. Hidden Killer is an easy one, and if the Talon isn't braindead they will likely be very quick to use it on humans they butcher. Another fantastic way that Red Talons defend their territory is through the use of Shadows of the Impergium. Very few humans have the mental wherewithal to remember anything with a -2 willpower penalty, and use of the gift is passive. A Shadow Lord in my current group learned it as a favor and now it is a relatively easy way to destroy the memory of witnesses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T15:57:31-08:00","id":1044241,"title":"","content":"something I've wondered...<br /> <br /> whats it like to be the only Callow Kin, or high Willpower individual to see a Garou, to have your sanity questioned by your own friends.<br /> <br /> when they were THERE too.<br /> <br /> or on a photograph<br /> <br /> when your coworkers are laughing it off as an obvious hoax.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T16:02:22-08:00","id":1044245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044241#post1044241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something I've wondered...<br /> <br /> whats it like to be the only Callow Kin, or high Willpower individual to see a Garou, to have your sanity questioned by your own friends.<br /> <br /> when they were THERE too.<br /> <br /> or on a photograph<br /> <br /> when your coworkers are laughing it off as an obvious hoax.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scary, I'd imagine. That's the sort of thing that makes the individual question whether or not they really saw what they think they saw. And after a while they will convince themselves that they are obviously wrong, and everyone else was right. It's got to be a lonely, terrifying time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T16:12:43-08:00","id":1044249,"title":"","content":"Which is one of the reasons why the Delirium is such a wonderful tool to the Garou. When everyone else just remembers a hairy maniac with two meat cleavers, your memories start to appear suspect, especially if the other witnesses are people you trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T16:34:35-08:00","id":1044267,"title":"","content":"Might work for Callow kin.<br /> <br /> but High willpower people probaly have stronger egos, thus victimizing them again<br /> <br /> they can either be quiet to keep their jobs and position in society... or become outcasts...<br /> <br /> sorry if im sounding too grim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T22:53:57-08:00","id":1044394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044028#post1044028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) Have fall guys ready. If there is a psycho on PCP ready at the time some Garou kill people, then unleash that psycho right now and have the police gun him down. That way the investigation ends quickly before all the evidence can be analyzed quickly. This is something the Bone Gnawer tribe might be good at - finding potential patsies to blame things on. Of course there would be some ethical dilemmas involved, but the Garou have done worse on the behalf of Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Even high-profile investigations will tend to be conducted much more sloppily if the apparent perpetrator is highly obvious -- and doubly so if he is dead and there is no reason to put together an air-tight case for a prosecution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Hidden Killer is an easy one, and if the Talon isn't braindead they will likely be very quick to use it on humans they butcher.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAlthough this is not perfect. The gift affects only the wounds, not inanimate objects -- like clothing or backpacks. Also, my interpretation of &quot;after a battle&quot; is that there is something of an unspecified time-limit to how long you can wait to use the gift. Coming back days later because only now is it obvious that covering one's tracks is vital (for instance the pack was a bunch of cubs and nobody knew the gift), seems unreasonable to me.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy solution: Grab the bodies, toss them off a cliff. They fell down the cliffside to their deaths (you would not believe the stupid sh** I've seen people do in the backcountry), and the bite wounds were the result of post-mortem animal predation. Case closed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T07:54:33-08:00","id":1044509,"title":"","content":"Well, there is still the problem of a Red Talon with a taste for long pig. You are looking at a future BSD recruitment because the Wyrm has already deeply touched him. He needs to go to Erebus for cleansing or else he will betray the Garou Nation, just like so many before him.<br /> <br /> The issue isn't the action necessarily, it is what the action is a symptom of. Cannibalism, casual murder, serial rape, etc are all symptoms of severe Wyrm taint. Unlike with humans though, Garou have a non-lethal option, Erebus. If they are unwilling to send the member to Erebus though, the member will be dancing the Spiral soon as the BSD are more his type of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:15:58-08:00","id":1044590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044509#post1044509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, there is still the problem of a Red Talon with a taste for long pig. You are looking at a future BSD recruitment because the Wyrm has already deeply touched him. He needs to go to Erebus for cleansing or else he will betray the Garou Nation, just like so many before him.</div> </div> </div> </div>In character, I can see this argument. OOC this is completely wrong. You are recommending Erebus like it's the logical next step. It isn't. Erebus is for cleansing severely screwed up Garou. For this, a Rite of Cleansing and a Punishment Rite is plenty for this sort of thing. And the Punishment Rite is really just (from the Talon Sept point of view) required because an outside Philodox is coming in because someone screwed up and drew undue attention to the Sept. If the behavior continues, then more severe punishments will/should be looked into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044509#post1044509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The issue isn't the action necessarily, it is what the action is a symptom of. Cannibalism, casual murder, serial rape, etc are all symptoms of severe Wyrm taint. Unlike with humans though, Garou have a non-lethal option, Erebus. If they are unwilling to send the member to Erebus though, the member will be dancing the Spiral soon as the BSD are more his type of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that logic, a good portion of the Talon Tribe should be BSDs. Since they're not (we know this factually) I conclude that you are mistaken.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:23:27-08:00","id":1044597,"title":"","content":"Ya I gotta agree, Garou are tragic, fallible, unstable beings. They are Monsters first before they are everything else.<br /> <br /> Furthermore , in WAR shit happens.....ALOT.<br /> <br /> And when stuff goes FUBAR, the missions success comes first before reprimands are handed out. Also the rank of the soldier and his contacts have a lot A lot more to do with what kind of punishment he or she is going to receive. If airing the fuck up would do more harm to the unit than it would to punish the offender, then it probably wont be brought to light so that the unit can save face and continue the war effort.<br /> <br /> Fuck ups are handled in house so to speak , unless the fuck up gets leaked. Red Talons don't strike me as &quot;leakers&quot; considering how insular they are.<br /> <br /> IMO- BSD's are evil, they serve evil and do evil things happily and readily.<br /> <br /> Gaian Garou commit evil acts in service to save and serve the greater good, and only start to slip when they start enjoying it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:36:46-08:00","id":1044604,"title":"","content":"The 'in war, shit happens' speech has a lot more weight among civilians than it does among those who served. For those of us who served, we know that there is a line that you do not cross without becoming the cautionary tale. The 'in war, shit happens' line to justify atrocities is just stuff said by civilians who never put themselves on the line and whose closest experience serving is playing Call of Duty on the PC.<br /> <br /> Yes, Fog of War happens and the wrong person is shot during a firefight. Yes, bullets travel far beyond line of sight and occasionally hit civilians. But dragging civilians out of their cars, executing them, and eating their corpse (which is the equivalent of what the Red Talon did in the above scenario) is a war crime and will be repeated if it is not dealt with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:37:16-08:00","id":1044605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044597#post1044597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ya I gotta agree, Garou are tragic, fallible, unstable beings. They are Monsters first before they are everything else.<br /> <br /> Furthermore , in WAR shit happens.....ALOT.<br /> <br /> And when stuff goes FUBAR, the missions success comes first before reprimands are handed out. Also the rank of the soldier and his contacts have a lot A lot more to do with what kind of punishment he or she is going to receive. If airing the fuck up would do more harm to the unit than it would to punish the offender, then it probably wont be brought to light so that the unit can save face and continue the war effort.<br /> <br /> Fuck ups are handled in house so to speak , unless the fuck up gets leaked. Red Talons don't strike me as &quot;leakers&quot; considering how insular they are.<br /> <br /> IMO- BSD's are evil, they serve evil and do evil things happily and readily.<br /> <br /> Gaian Garou commit evil acts in service to save and serve the greater good, and only start to slip when they start enjoying it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Evil&quot; is kind of a useless term (imo) in general in the WoD, but I get what you're saying.<br /> <br /> I've been in a pack where someone ended up eating a person. We handled it in-pack specifically for the reasons you mentioned above. We kicked his teeth in and made sure he understood that if it ever happened again, he was going to be turned over to the Sept for as severe a punishment as we could argue for. And that was the end of it. That packmate was really careful from then on. And by us not turning him in, it actually built up pack cohesiveness.<br /> Garou society isn't &quot;nice&quot; by any stretch of the imagination. And the fact that Garou regenerate means that physical punishments can be handed out with little after-effects. Disputes can also be handled quickly and painfully and as long as no one loses control and attacks using natural weaponry (Agg) it's all good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044604#post1044604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But dragging civilians out of their cars, executing them, and eating their corpse (which is the equivalent of what the Red Talon did in the above scenario) is a war crime and will be repeated if it is not dealt with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, to the Talons those humans aren't &quot;civilians&quot;. They are the enemy. And it doesn't sound like they dragged the hikers out of their cars. I would guess the college students wandered into their territory. It's a slight difference, but it matters for motivation.<br /> <br /> That's kind of the point. And the eating the flesh of humans isn't a &quot;war crime&quot; to them. It's a rule handed down by their leaders that they don't necessarily agree with. Even still, for the most part the Red Talons do abide by it because of that.<br /> They just don't see breaking that (to them) useless law as all that big of a deal. And so they will handle it themselves. The reason this scenario will be a bigger deal to them is because an outside Philodox (the CoG) now has to come in to address it.<br /> <br /> This would be a similar scenario to a Philodox showing up to a Gnawer Caern to address a Metis birth. The Gnawers don't see that particular law as being as big of a deal as most of the Tribes do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 02-06-2017, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T11:29:07-08:00","id":1044633,"title":"","content":"Democritus isn't going to throw the offenders into Erebus, unless the humans were killed in some Wyrm Ritual. While the old wolf is a traditionalist, being CoG, he is more focused on Rehabilitation than punishment. He will protect the Veil and investigate to find the root cause of the breach.<br /> <br /> If subjecting the offenders to a punishment right will make sure they never break the litany again, he will conduct the rite. If separating the pack and sending them to different septs will stop the crimes, then he will do that. If replacing the Sept Alpha with another wolf who takes the Litany more seriously, that's what he will do. If having the offending Red Talon run with him so Democritus could teach him the wisdom and honor he lacks, the old wolf will drag that poor Red Talon with him while he travels the Garou Nation. It's not the first time he has done this with a Litany Breaker Democritus believes has potential.<br /> <br /> (Man, I really derailed this topic. Sorry guys)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-06-2017, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T11:48:21-08:00","id":1044637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044633#post1044633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Democritus isn't going to throw the offenders into Erebus. While the old wolf is a traditionalist, being CoG, he is more focused on Rehabilitation than punishment. He will protect the Veil and investigate to find the root cause of the breach.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Garou that isn't insanely hard line would decide to send the offender to Erebus, so that's good to hear. I doubt a CoG would be capable of it anyways, without actually escorting said Garou there. The Punishment Rite to send someone there is specifically a Silverfang one if I remember correctly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044633#post1044633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If subjecting the offenders to a punishment right will make sure they never break the litany again, he will conduct the rite. If separating the pack and sending them to different septs will stop the crimes, then he will do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was completely with you up to this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044633#post1044633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If replacing the Sept Alpha with another wolf who takes the Litany more seriously, that's what he will do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something he does not (and will never) have the authority to do. Replacing a Sept Alpha will require either going to war with the Caern and taking it from the Talons by force, or getting a Rival within the Sept to challenge and take it themselves. Neither of these options seem likely. Especially not from a CoG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044633#post1044633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If having the offending Red Talon run with him so Democritus could teach him the wisdom and honor he lacks, the old wolf will drag that poor Red Talon with him while he travels the Garou Nation. It's not the first time he has done this with a Litany Breaker Democritus believes has potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>This option is an interesting one, but again, won't happen without the consent of the Sept Leader(s). That really is the biggest issue here. And one I see going over pretty well actually. Your NPC needs to get the Sept Elders on his side. And they should be inclined to do so, because it will benefit them greatly to make sure this kind of attention isn't drawn to them again. It's just a matter of being politically persuasive. And since this is all being handled by NPCs anyways, there is no reason to assuming the COG isn't equipped skills-wise to do what needs to be done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044633#post1044633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (Man, I really derailed this topic. Sorry guys)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you did really. All of this pertains directly to the OP's topic, and he has participated right along with the rest of us, so it's all good. I've had fun discussing this at length.<br /> <br /> And as long as you're here (since this is your scenario), a few clarification questions:<br /> How many Talons were involved in eating people? Was it a whole pack, or just a couple of the pack members? If it was only a few, did the others know?<br /> Where were the hikers attacked? How close is that to the Caern/Protectorate?<br /> What level is the Caern/how many Garou are present?<br /> What does the leadership/Sept positions of the Caern look like (Rank/Auspice-wise)?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T12:10:19-08:00","id":1044648,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the information on what an Outside Garou can and cannot do. I'm still trying to get all the little details about the Garou nation down.<br /> <br /> I'm going to use this for my quest, so I rather not get into details. There may be players on the board. Also, I haven't gotten the Red Talon sept nailed down yet. This plot, if I decide to do it will come at the last part of the quest.<br /> <br /> I suppose I can give you <i>some</i> details. They may change. <br /> <br /> The Hikers strayed too close to the Red Talons territory.<br /> The Caern is most likely going to be level three? I'm looking for a mid sized Caern. I'm still not sure about the Caern levels and what they mean.<br /> The Sept Leadership is going to be very welcoming of the Lupus Garou. Not so much of the Homid and Metis garou. I'm not sure if I'm going to have Democritus bring the non-Lupus members along or just leave them in town. Even if they are left in town, he will inform the Red Talon leadership they are there. <br /> <br /> In town, there is a Metis CoG Park Ranger living in a Trailer with her Kinfolk Wolf mate. This Metis will be the contact for the PC's pack. She is not all that social, but understand the need to not ignore the Human world. The Sept threw her out for interacting in the Human world but damn it, someone has to do it. The local humans aren't sure what to make of this weirdo hairless Park Ranger that has a &quot;pet wolf&quot;. <br /> <br /> I really just wanted a plot involving litany breaking that wasn't &quot;I'm working for the Wyrm now&quot; or a First Litany breach. Red Talons eating people and drawing too much attention to themselves just seemed to be an obvious plot. <br /> <br /> The idea popped into my head when this old wolf, who never watches TV, is suddenly paying CNN a lot of attention. He hushes everyone when news talks about two lost college girls. Someone says they hope the girls alive. <br /> <br /> &quot;No, They won't be found.&quot;<br /> &quot;Why?&quot;<br /> &quot;They are digesting in a Red Talon's stomach.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T12:13:13-08:00","id":1044649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044604#post1044604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 'in war, shit happens' speech has a lot more weight among civilians than it does among those who served. For those of us who served, we know that there is a line that you do not cross without becoming the cautionary tale. The 'in war, shit happens' line to justify atrocities is just stuff said by civilians who never put themselves on the line and whose closest experience serving is playing Call of Duty on the PC.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Man I call big time BS on all that.<br /> <br /> I don't want to derail this topic but I cant let this slide, and I have got to say , if the insinuation was that I didn't serve your wrong.<br /> <br /> Secondly, You know when I got back and tried to rationalize some shit and had to play what happened over sometimes to help myself and &quot;civilians &quot; understand what kinda shit goes down.....the LAST THING any civilian muttered was &quot; In War Shit happens!&quot; <br /> <br /> Civilians don't say that?!?!<br /> <br /> You know who does say that?---&gt; Veterans shooting the shit trying to rationalize horrible times over a beer....<br /> <br /> You know who bitches about beauracratic page flipping that ends up putting you in danger ---&gt; Officers looking to make their stripes on the backs of enlisted men and women trying to get back home safely<br /> <br /> You know who cites &quot;rules and regulations&quot; and how you &quot;should have or shouldn't have&quot; done something, when they themselves have no frame of reference to the fucked up shit that goes on when boots hit the ground ----&gt; .......Civilians.......Hipsters....College Kids<br /> <br /> ok Im done<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T12:17:27-08:00","id":1044653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044633#post1044633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Democritus isn't going to throw the offenders into Erebus, unless the humans were killed in some Wyrm Ritual. While the old wolf is a traditionalist, being CoG, he is more focused on Rehabilitation than punishment. He will protect the Veil and investigate to find the root cause of the breach.<br /> <br /> If subjecting the offenders to a punishment right will make sure they never break the litany again, he will conduct the rite. If separating the pack and sending them to different septs will stop the crimes, then he will do that. If replacing the Sept Alpha with another wolf who takes the Litany more seriously, that's what he will do. If having the offending Red Talon run with him so Democritus could teach him the wisdom and honor he lacks, the old wolf will drag that poor Red Talon with him while he travels the Garou Nation. It's not the first time he has done this with a Litany Breaker Democritus believes has potential.<br /> <br /> (Man, I really derailed this topic. Sorry guys)</div> </div> </div> </div>Back on topic I see it like this.<br /> <br /> A college kid full of ideals and visions about how &quot;society&quot; should be gets word that a group of skinheads is hanging down at a local park and messing people up (for various extremist beliefs that they have adopted outside of &quot;normal&quot; society)....college kid ready to defend his ideals walks down to the park running over in his head how he is going to approach this. He shows up outnumbered with an idealogy that is the Polar Opposite of the gang of skinheads he is &quot;coming to correct&quot;. How do you think that would play out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T12:31:43-08:00","id":1044664,"title":"","content":"Hm, it depends on the capabilities and savagery of the college kid. If he is a normal college kid, he is probably going to be looking for dentures when he gets out of the hospital in the best case scenario. If he is a trained martial artist (and I do not mean someone who is trained in an art or sport style but someone trained in a combat style) and he is savage enough to bring weapons and to go for the kill, he might be able to get out of the park without being sent to the hospital or being brought up on charges (especially if he is smart enough to look up to local rules concerning self-defense and justifiable homicide). I would suggest that he get a concealed carry license (and liability insurance) and actually know how to shoot and retain a revolver before he goes down there though, as he should expect escalation and be willing to shoot to kill if they try to attack him because they will probably swarm him and stomp him flat if he comes in with a gun and appears to be afraid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T13:24:05-08:00","id":1044690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044245#post1044245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scary, I'd imagine. That's the sort of thing that makes the individual question whether or not they really saw what they think they saw. And after a while they will convince themselves that they are obviously wrong, and everyone else was right. It's got to be a lonely, terrifying time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hmmn how do you think it would be if your an investigator, lawyer or police officer.<br /> <br /> if you KNOW theirs more going on then meets the eye...<br /> <br /> Anyone played Yakuza 1? it has something like that early on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T14:43:16-08:00","id":1044730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044648#post1044648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thanks for the information on what an Outside Garou can and cannot do. I'm still trying to get all the little details about the Garou nation down.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might help to think of each Sept as a separate city-state. Combined they make up the &quot;Garou Nation&quot; but that's really only because they share the same Litany have (theoretically) have the same goals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044648#post1044648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm going to use this for my quest, so I rather not get into details. There may be players on the board. Also, I haven't gotten the Red Talon sept nailed down yet. This plot, if I decide to do it will come at the last part of the quest.<br /> <br /> I suppose I can give you <i>some</i> details. They may change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was just curious to understand how this had played out. No need to possibly compromise your storyline for my curiosity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044648#post1044648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hikers strayed too close to the Red Talons territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>This setup made the most sense, but I realized when someone said &quot;pulled them from their car&quot; that it had never actually been stated how this happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044648#post1044648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Caern is most likely going to be level three? I'm looking for a mid sized Caern. I'm still not sure about the Caern levels and what they mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quoted this in the other thread, but here's a slightly expanded one (to include levels 2 and 3):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Players Handbook 2nd Ed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Rank 2</b><br /> Average Population: From 8 to 15 Garou<br /> Average Bawn: 200-350 acres<br /> Maximum Moon Bridge Distance: 2,000 miles<br /> Gauntlet: 4<br /> Advantages: Relatively little politicking; packs can acquire healthy totem spirits; may have a chance to fill a minor Sept position.<br /> Disadvantages: Still not much raw power; small Bawn for living space; still cramped for Lupus; few defenders if attacked.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 3</b><br /> Average Population: From 10 to 20 Garou<br /> Average Bawn: 350-800 acres<br /> Maximum Moon Bridge Distance: 3,000 miles<br /> Gauntlet: 3<br /> Advantages: Source of significant power; relatively easy to access spirits and mentors; reliable allies within Sept mates<br /> Disadvantages: AlMost no chance for inexperienced Garou to fill any Sept positions; defence is tricky due to larger size of Bawn; enough Garou for politics and in fighting; large enough to come to the Wyrm\u2019s attention; difficult to expand or maintain properly.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044648#post1044648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I really just wanted a plot involving litany breaking that wasn't &quot;I'm working for the Wyrm now&quot; or a First Litany breach. Red Talons eating people and drawing too much attention to themselves just seemed to be an obvious plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>This setup nails that perfectly. It sounds like it will be a lot of fun to play through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044690#post1044690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmn how do you think it would be if your an investigator, lawyer or police officer.<br /> <br /> if you KNOW theirs more going on then meets the eye...<br /> <br /> Anyone played Yakuza 1? it has something like that early on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't played that game, but I would imagine the person would be a lot quieter about it. Better to keep that to yourself than alienate yourself when speaking to others. I can see them trying to figure out exactly what's going on. They will be going it alone, and should be justifiably paranoid, the more they learn. There will still be plenty of time to doubt themselves, but I don't think it will be as glaring as with more &quot;normal&quot; people. Knowing they are alone in their search might even feed their motivation to find out more.<br /> <br /> Those are the types of people that can go on to become dangerous to the Supernatural communities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T15:20:08-08:00","id":1044744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044730#post1044730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might help to think of each Sept as a separate city-state. Combined they make up the &quot;Garou Nation&quot; but that's really only because they share the same Litany have (theoretically) have the same goals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, I was just curious to understand how this had played out. No need to possibly compromise your storyline for my curiosity.<br /> <br /> <br /> This setup made the most sense, but I realized when someone said &quot;pulled them from their car&quot; that it had never actually been stated how this happened.<br /> <br /> <br /> I quoted this in the other thread, but here's a slightly expanded one (to include levels 2 and 3):<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This setup nails that perfectly. It sounds like it will be a lot of fun to play through.<br /> <br /> <br /> Haven't played that game, but I would imagine the person would be a lot quieter about it. Better to keep that to yourself than alienate yourself when speaking to others. I can see them trying to figure out exactly what's going on. They will be going it alone, and should be justifiably paranoid, the more they learn. There will still be plenty of time to doubt themselves, but I don't think it will be as glaring as with more &quot;normal&quot; people. Knowing they are alone in their search might even feed their motivation to find out more.<br /> <br /> Those are the types of people that can go on to become dangerous to the Supernatural communities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> early in the game the protaganist frames himself for murder (to shield a guy who murdered someone for sexually asaulting his sister.<br /> <br /> Well one cop could see the guy making a confession was covering for someone... but his superiors decided to just call it a day and conclude the investigation.<br /> <br /> Not sure if he shows up again or not...only made it so far.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T16:48:04-08:00","id":1044771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044604#post1044604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Fog of War happens and the wrong person is shot during a firefight. Yes, bullets travel far beyond line of sight and occasionally hit civilians....</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAgree. Accidents happen (especially in a chaotic environment where everybody has weapons and combatants and civvies are all mixed in with each other), but there's a massive difference between an accident by a 19-year-old PFC, hyped up on adrenaline and scared out of his mind, and cold-blooded murder. Civilians have (understandably, in my opinion) a hard time conceptualizing that making good decisions is far easier when nobody is trying to kill you while you're making it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044604#post1044604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But dragging civilians out of their cars, executing them, and eating their corpse (which is the equivalent of what the Red Talon did in the above scenario) is a war crime and will be repeated if it is not dealt with.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDragging civilians out of their cars and shooting them in the head is a war crime... <i>eating</i> them is probably more appropriately dealt with by assigning the offender a nice, padded cell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T08:20:08-08:00","id":1045073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1043865-repairing-the-veil?p=1044771#post1044771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAgree. Accidents happen (especially in a chaotic environment where everybody has weapons and combatants and civvies are all mixed in with each other), but there's a massive difference between an accident by a 19-year-old PFC, hyped up on adrenaline and scared out of his mind, and cold-blooded murder. Civilians have (understandably, in my opinion) a hard time conceptualizing that making good decisions is far easier when nobody is trying to kill you while you're making it.<br /> <br /> \u200bDragging civilians out of their cars and shooting them in the head is a war crime... <i>eating</i> them is probably more appropriately dealt with by assigning the offender a nice, padded cell.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshio_Tachibana\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/19/Yoshio_Tachibana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshio_Tachibana\" target=\"_blank\"> Yoshio Tachibana - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.